            <ArticleTitle>Identification of potent, soluble, and orally active TRPV1 antagonists.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2559-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2011.01.112</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Optimization of a water soluble, moderately potent lead series of isoxazole-3-carboxamides was conducted, affording a compound with the requisite balance of potency, solubility and physicochemical properties for in vivo use. Compound 8e was demonstrated to be efficacious in a rat model of inflammatory pain, following oral administration.</AbstractText>
